        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Königgrätz</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">3 July 1866</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near the Bohemian city of Hradec Králové (Königgrätz) and the village of Sadová, between the Bystřice and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">Wilhelm I</a>, with the Army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> (39,000) under Herwarth von Bittenfeld, the First Army (85,000) under Prince Friedrich Karl and the Second Army (almost 100,000) under Crown Prince Frederick William, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> allies under Ludwig von Benedek, 215,000 men in the battle</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Austrian army was forced to retreat across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> with roughly 31,000 men killed, wounded or missing, against nearly 9,000 on the Prussian side. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> went on to win the war.</span></div>
